Pooka programming language <version>
Objects belong on the BEAM too.

Usage: pooka <command> [arguments]

Commands:
  new <name>                          Create a new Pooka project
  check [--verbose] [--json] [--fix]  Check the project for errors
  build [--target dev|prod]           Type check and compile the project to BEAM
  run [-- <arguments>]                Build and execute main()
  test [--verbose|--compact]          Compile and execute the project's tests
  format [--check] [<file.pooka>...]  Format Pooka source code
  docs                                Generate documentation for the project
  add <package[@version]> [options]   Add a dependency
  remove <package>                    Remove a dependency
  deps <command>                      Manage dependencies
  export <escript|shipment|release>   Export an escript, production shipment or OTP release
  publish [options]                   Prepare or publish a package and documentation to Hex
  clean                               Remove build artifacts
  -h, --help                          Print this help
  -V, --version                       Print the version

Run `pooka <command> --help` for command-specific usage.

